(5121060, 746161, 34938, '<td valign="top">Looks wonderful, has a really earthy tone to it</td>', 'Looks wonderful, has a really earthy tone to it', '2008-12-10 00:08:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(5121090, 746169, 28359, '<td valign="top">To cute...Love it!</td>', 'To cute...Love it!', '2008-12-10 00:14:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(5121104, 746127, 96915, '<td valign="top">Awww I have a border collie sweetheart too :)  Unfortunately this isn''t a very dynamic image.  Nice colors and textures in the pebbles though.</td>', 'Awww I have a border collie sweetheart too :)  Unfortunately this isn''t a very dynamic image.  Nice colors and textures in the pebbles though.', '2008-12-10 00:17:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(5121112, 746047, 34938, '<td valign="top">front page potential...well done 8</td>', 'front page potential...well done 8', '2008-12-10 00:19:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(5121146, 746184, 34938, '<td valign="top">great portrait...beautiful smile and face...perfect for the challenge 8</td>', 'great portrait...beautiful smile and face...perfect for the challenge 8', '2008-12-10 00:30:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(5121154, 746196, 63633, '<td valign="top">This is lovely, but I don''t see how you have used flash in this. I may be ignorant, and if so, I''m sorry.</td>', 'This is lovely, but I don''t see how you have used flash in this. I may be ignorant, and if so, I''m sorry.', '2008-12-10 00:33:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(5121165, 746038, 96881, '<td valign="top">Just having a quick look at all thumbnails and this jumped out.  Exactly what I thought should be presented in the challenge. Subject is naturally backlit, photo exposed for the sky and surrounding landscape, and the subject then correctly exposed through the use of fill flash.  Perfect match for the challenge.<br/>Might be a little too closely cropped both top and bottom, but that is just me.<br/>Great Submission.  Really Stood out</td>', 'Just having a quick look at all thumbnails and this jumped out.  Exactly what I thought should be presented in the challenge. Subject is naturally backlit, photo exposed for the sky and surrounding landscape, and the subject then correctly exposed through the use of fill flash.  Perfect match for the challenge.Might be a little too closely cropped both top and bottom, but that is just me.Great Submission.  Really Stood out', '2008-12-10 00:38:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(5121175, 746047, 96881, '<td valign="top">Great capture for the challenge.  Good use of fill light to highlight the subject. The white might be a tiny bit overexposed though when being fussy.  Sky looks great.   The little red is good. The border works.  Great submission here.</td>', 'Great capture for the challenge.  Good use of fill light to highlight the subject. The white might be a tiny bit overexposed though when being fussy.  Sky looks great.   The little red is good. The border works.  Great submission here.', '2008-12-10 00:41:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(5121185, 746184, 27133, '<td valign="top">Smile Jaime!</td>', 'Smile Jaime!', '2008-12-10 00:44:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(5121190, 745852, 96881, '<td valign="top">I thought this challenge was perfect for Family Portraits (from someone who normally hates them), yet few people have gone this way.  Exposed for the sky effects and then use fill flash to correctly expose the subject.  Seems easy.<br/>The boy is a little dark, comes from being behind the girl, especially when the light is coming from the left.  Also, i think the light needed to be slightly (read slightly....._ more central, just enough to move that shaddow just off their eyes.<br/>I have taken many kids photos, and get sick of saying ''drop your chin slightly'', but I think a light drop of the chin (to match the girls) for the boy also would have been good.<br/>I know, small things, and yes, being a little picky, but that isn''t affecting your score.  Just trying to help and see if next time, you can get that perfect shot........well done</td>', 'I thought this challenge was perfect for Family Portraits (from someone who normally hates them), yet few people have gone this way.  Exposed for the sky effects and then use fill flash to correctly expose the subject.  Seems easy.The boy is a little dark, comes from being behind the girl, especially when the light is coming from the left.  Also, i think the light needed to be slightly (read slightly....._ more central, just enough to move that shaddow just off their eyes.I have taken many kids photos, and get sick of saying ''drop your chin slightly'', but I think a light drop of the chin (to match the girls) for the boy also would have been good.I know, small things, and yes, being a little picky, but that isn''t affecting your score.  Just trying to help and see if next time, you can get that perfect shot........well done', '2008-12-10 00:47:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(5121219, 746046, 96881, '<td valign="top">I can see the use of fill in flash here, but I am not sure it is trully adding to the picture.  The lit grass does little for me, nor does the lower half of the tree.  The bright white on the horizon also detracts from the overall view</td>', 'I can see the use of fill in flash here, but I am not sure it is trully adding to the picture.  The lit grass does little for me, nor does the lower half of the tree.  The bright white on the horizon also detracts from the overall view', '2008-12-10 00:57:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(5121250, 746084, 90098, '<td valign="top">I think this would look awesome in black and white.  Nice photo nonetheless.</td>', 'I think this would look awesome in black and white.  Nice photo nonetheless.', '2008-12-10 01:09:39.000000', NULL, 1),
